  "findings": [
    {
      "area": "Exact-coprime centre and moving endpoints",
      "result": "PASS",
      "source": "P4BPositiveUpperPrimeBV.lean:34-115",
      "detail": "primeError is the actual prime congruence count minus the exact q-coprime prime count divided by phi(q). Its displayed identity keeps E_li(Y,a,q)-E_li(Y,1,1)/phi(q)+primeDivisorCount(Y,q)/phi(q). The q=1 pi/li term is not omitted. The trueLi normalization is 2/log(2)+integral from 2, not the proxy x/log(x). The imported nested prefix maximum handles independently moving integer Y(q)<=X and every primitive residue a(q)."
    },
    {
      "area": "Finite correction budgets and logarithmic payment",
      "result": "PASS_RELATIVE_TO_CLASSICAL_BV",
      "source": "P4BPositiveUpperPrimeBV.lean:85-200",
      "detail": "Squarefree positive S in [1,Q] gives the exact finite bound (1+4H(Q))*bvPool(X,Q)+4H(Q)^2. The full prime-divisor correction uses actual q=p*(q/p), squarefreeness and totient multiplicativity before enlarging the quotient carrier; no endpoint-only correction is substituted. For Q=floor(X^(9/20)), the genuine log-loss cutoff comparison uses epsilon=1/20. Classical BV at A+2 and eventual log^(A+2)(X)<=X give C_A=9*C_BV+16. Constants and threshold precede S,Y,a."
    },
    {
      "area": "Signed profiles",
      "result": "PASS_RELATIVE_TO_CLASSICAL_BV",
      "source": "P4BPositiveUpperPrimeBV.lean:202-258",
      "detail": "The exact profile on one common prime carrier is sum_i c_i*1_(p<=Y_i). Linearity, the literal prefix restriction identity and finite Fubini give payment by sum_i |c_i|, with no extra endpoint-cardinality factor. This includes signed intervals. It proves no total-variation or Fourier bound for the actual smooth Gamma charts, and no convolution estimate."
    },
    {
      "area": "Actual original upper coefficient",
      "result": "PASS_RELATIVE_TO_CLASSICAL_BV",
      "source": "P2OriginalGammaUpperPrimeBVAttachment.lean:21-134",
      "detail": "The whole displayed carrier is reduced exactly to activeLow. Actual J support derives q>0, squarefreeness, target-coprimality, scalar one and q<N^(19/48+epsilon)<=N^(9/20), retaining full beta and exact r=19/96. The prime-profile threshold is before all policies, caps, nu,epsilon and profiles. No lower ALL16 W source or rank199 capacity is used."
    },
    {
      "area": "Complete local scale and threshold",
      "result": "PASS_WITH_EXPLICIT_SOURCE_HYPOTHESES",
      "source": "P2OriginalGammaUpperPrimeBVAttachment.lean:142-190",
      "detail": "J actual ordered tuples, block ownership, complete trim and support give x>=N^(1-kappa0)/4 and active q<x^(9/20). For a natural prime cap X>=x, power growth forces X beyond the classical BV threshold using a single N0 before X,N, tuples, blocks, policy, cap, primitive residue selector and profile. The error stays C_A*X/log^A(X), not a claimed error at a shorter prime fibre. No upper bound on X or full smooth-atlas producer is supplied."
    },
    {
      "area": "Moving residue and exact complements",
      "result": "PASS",
      "source": "P2OriginalGammaUpperPrimeBVAttachment.lean:34-91,192-209",
      "detail": "The generic Bezout residue identity is valid for every complementary integer b. If (b,q)>1, congruence and exact mean both vanish because (N,q)=1; otherwise the residue is primitive. The actual label identity keeps b=t.1*t.2 and residual x.1.prod*x.2, never declaring that residual prime. The full mother list and unit quotient x.2=1 survive. fullError retains both low unit/nonunit terms and highError. RootQ, marked scalar and Theta are unchanged."
    }
  ],
